# Sequential offline scope failures and recovery. Planning starts no scan jobs.
name: Unsupported discovery scope, readable failure and explicit revision
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/discovery_scope.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
wait-for: 25 Start Map
submit: use sast
wait-for: 15 TOOLS
submit: options sast:scan
wait-for: 15 sast:scan
submit: set taskMode manual
submit: set tasks secret-scan
submit: set paths service/app.py
submit: scan batch
wait-for: 20 PLAN A STUDY
keys: L
require-live-snap: 15 Study draft unavailable | file-scope-refused
expect: requires directory scopes
expect: No scan started
ask: Does the form explain that the selected file is unsupported without silently enlarging discovery, and provide a way to revise it?
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/discovery_scope.py @TMP_TARGET @ART blocked
resize: 160x48
live-snap: scope-160x48
ask: At 160x48, are the blocked scope, its reason and recovery controls understandable with no approval implied?
resize: 96x89
live-snap: scope-96x89
ask: At 96x89, is the selected file still attached to the failure rather than presented as an accepted scope?
resize: 80x24
live-snap: scope-80x24
ask: At 80x24, can the operator read the refusal and reach the rest of its guidance using the visible controls?
resize: 60x20
live-snap: scope-60x20
ask: At 60x20, are the failed draft and paging/back controls preserved?
resize: 40x12
live-snap: scope-40x12
ask: At 40x12, can the operator recognize the failed draft and page through its full explanation without losing the form?
keys: NPage
live-snap: scope-40x12-paged
expect: directory and review
ask: Can the operator reach the scope recovery instructions at 40x12?
resize: 120x36
keys: Escape
submit: options sast:scan
wait-for: 15 sast:scan
submit: set paths service
submit: scan batch
wait-for: 20 PLAN A STUDY
keys: L
require-live-snap: 30 Draft ready | revised-directory-draft
expect: No jobs started
ask: Does explicitly choosing the larger directory create a new draft for review while preserving three passes and one worker, without starting discovery?
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/discovery_scope.py @TMP_TARGET @ART draft
keys: C-c
wait-for: 10 CONFIRM SESSION EXIT
keys: y
require-exit: 10
resize: 120x36
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
wait-for: 25 Start Map
submit: use sast
submit: options sast:scan
submit: set taskMode manual
submit: set tasks secret-scan
submit: set paths service/app.py
submit: scan batch
wait-for: 20 PLAN A STUDY
keys: L
require-live-snap: 15 Study draft unavailable | scope-no-color
expect: requires directory scopes
ask: Is the unsupported scope and its recovery readable without color, with the previous draft left separate?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
